{"kind":"request","text":"AE-1: one archive driver for every room Worker. Part of the\nstable base, under order fc7576f8.\n\nThe fact at main 57e893c0. Only the Grow Worker archives a room.\n`apps/room/worker.grow.ts` wires `archiveHost` and `archive`, and\n`apps/room/archive-policy.ts` admits two signed Grow definitions\nand five platform pins. The Workers that use `apps/room/worker.ts`\nrun no archive. `docs/operate-a-service.md` states the limit:\n\"Today the archive engine runs only for the demo room on the\nhosted `dap-grow` Worker.\" A room asks for an archive with the\ndirectory act `bind-archive`, and the default family of CF-1\nincludes the archive binding.\n\nOutcome: a room on any deployed room Worker that has an archive\nbinding archives its journals, and replay verifies the clone.\n\nWork:\n1. One archive driver that `worker.ts` and `worker.grow.ts`\n   share. It serves each directory that holds an archive\n   binding. It has no setting that names one directory.\n2. Policies come from the platform catalog and from the\n   declarations of each installed package. The engine still\n   admits only a definition that has a policy.\n3. A room with host `none` has no archive. Its pages say so.\n4. `docs/operate-a-service.md` gains a section \"Verify a room\n   from its archive\": `dap clone \u003cdir\u003e --archive`, then\n   `artroom-replay --git \u003cclone\u003e --all --expect-journals N\n   --json`, with the journal count from an independent list of\n   scopes.\n\nWitness: a room that is not the Grow room, with an installed\npackage, archives in a scope test, and `artroom-replay --all`\npasses on its clone. The Grow witness keeps its answers.\n\nBefore source edits, send me one act: where the driver lives,\nhow it finds the policy of an installed package, and each\nsetting of `wrangler.grow.jsonc` that goes.\n\nNot in AE-1: a restore. No deployment by the builder. After the\ncutover deployment I send `bind-archive` for each new room and\nrun the verificati